{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>ביום —</b> A great sage, author of a distinguished book, but it contains errors, said: כי ידי מקום עיני (my hands are the place of my eyes), and this is impossible for a man of understanding to say such a thing, even in idle talk, all the more so in the holy books. Some say: כי ידי (my hands) — my strength and power melted, as though it flowed, by way of metaphor, like וימסו אסוריו (his bonds melted), or it lacks a bet, as though it were בידי (in my hand) on account of my blow and affliction." "<b>לילה נגרה —</b> My cry, for above it is written ואצעקה (and I cried), and behold there is a cry there. And had it not been written, it would be like וברך ברכה (and he blessed a blessing), ולא אשיבנה, and many like this, and it is a way of metaphor, like ויתכו כמים שאגותי (my roarings poured like water). Or the meaning of ידי מקומי is my place, like ויד תהיה לך (and a hand shall be for you). And the meaning: his place flowed on account of his tears, therefore after it מאנה להנחם נפשי (my soul refused comfort), like ודמעתה על לחייה אין לה מנחם (her tears are on her cheeks, she has no comforter)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 77, :notes {0 "Resolved the unnamed sage as 'a great sage' without inserting an identity, since Ibn Ezra does not name him and the reference is uncertain.", 1 "Ibn Ezra's syntax in the second half is compressed and elliptical; translated hyper-literally without supplying connective tissue."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:49.669613083Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}